      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a vehicle arrives at its destination, the delivery handover is a structured procedure designed to verify that the automobile remains in the same condition as when it left the depot. The process begins with a daylight condition re‑inspection that is compared to the original pickup photographs. The delivery agent uses a calibrated camera to capture high‑resolution images of the vehicle’s exterior and interior from the same angles that were documented at pickup. These images are immediately uploaded to the central system where an automated comparison algorithm flags any discrepancies, such as new scratches, dents, or fluid leaks. The agent then reviews the flagged items in real time, noting the exact location and severity, and documents any findings</div>
